lines=['# V2 methodology and decision','',verdict+'. No submission, upload or publication was made.','', '## Verified baseline','V1 reproduces byte for byte in a clean Python 3.12.13 environment in 59.13 seconds. Mean fold AP is 0.5448294042; pooled OOF AP is 0.5371864804. Those are distinct local estimates, not a leaderboard score. See baseline_reproduction_report.md and its JSON evidence.','', '## Finite development experiments',table.to_string(index=False),'', '## Frozen confirmation',c.to_string(index=False),'', '## Acceptance evidence',json.dumps(v,indent=2),'', '## Interpretation','The depth-only changes test tree interaction capacity without changing observations. Local counterparty turnover and strict chronological value-compatible event chains test a specific feature hypothesis. Static graph ablation isolates static connectivity from the augmented behaviour block; local turnover and chronology were tested together, so gains cannot be attributed to either individually. No GNN, propagation, pseudo labels, calibration, score jitter or blend was justified by these results. LightGBM was not added: the finite comparison used linear regularization and two meaningful CatBoost capacity changes; cross-library tuning was deferred.','', '## Validation limits','Track A has no annotation-group overlap but all 700 wallets are shared and 33% of validation directed pairs repeat in fit. Track B has no supervised endpoint overlap, while full authorized unlabelled context and some annotation groups remain shared. One connected component prevents a meaningful graph-component split. Track C uses earlier labels and later labels but full seven-day offline context, so it does not establish causal detection. Reserved B1 is opened only when the primary threshold is met; otherwise it remains untouched. Conditional paired group bootstrap does not include retraining uncertainty; two seeds and limited partitions are not hidden-test proof. The primary folds were reused for five development experiments.','', '## Difficulty, edge cases and unresolved risk','All candidates retain medium/hard weaknesses; candidate_difficulty_comparison.csv measures the same positive categories and common negative set across models. High-scoring legitimate relays are a recurring false-positive source. Twenty-five hard positives deliberately have no distinguishable signal. Asset conversions remain one customer payment; LP legs are not counted as laundering hops. Amount matching uses reference valuations and actual first-leg cost, not SendMax or cross-asset nominal equality. Ordered matching is a candidate event chain, not proof of exact token provenance or end-to-end conservation. Simultaneous events are not ordered. Missing-history stress physically removes 30% of economic events; confirmation_results.csv compares the same retained targets with full and reduced context. Negative stress deltas are operational limitations, not hidden-test performance. Batch patterns absent from training, different graph density, novel wallets, lawful hubs and only seven days of context remain material risks.','', '## Reproduction and release','See source_v2/README.md for exact clean-workspace commands. Pin dependencies and four CPU threads. Source/configuration and aggregate evidence are packaged separately from raw data, fitted weights and per-transaction OOF files. v2_predictions.csv is created only after promotion and clean reproduction; failed acceptance means none is produced. V1 artifacts remain unchanged. Public terms were fetched from https://hackathon.ukcbt.org/terms on 24 October 2026: original material must be public by deadline, and team/captain/member, repository-version and AI/model/prompt/settings disclosures are required. Publication remains blocked by the user instruction, not silently performed. Fill submission identity/version metadata before an approved release. This research package is not a completed public entry.']
